**Reproduced** — 5 of 6 documented word forms failed: `is greater than`, `is less than`, `is greater than or equal to`, `is less than or equal to`, `is equal to` → `ParserError: Expected Then but got Identifier("than")` / `got To`. Only `is not` worked. Cause was `src/parser.rs:1308` looking past `TokenKind::Is` for only `=`/`not`.

**Red first** — `tests/comparison_words_test.rs::the_six_word_comparison_forms_parse_and_select_the_branch_they_name` failed with `Parser("Expected Then but got Identifier(\"than\")", Span { line: 3, column: 17 })` before any production change.

**Fix** (`src/parser.rs` +94 −18) — new `parse_is_operator` matches the word forms by name (the same technique `parse_has` uses for `default`), consuming `or equal to` as one phrase so it binds inside the comparison. A word counts as an operator only when the whole phrase is present, so `greater`/`less`/`equal`/`than` still work as variable names.

**Tests** — 13 new `#[test]` (10 `edge_*`) + 6 Redblue `test` blocks. Mutation-checked: forcing `or_equal_to_ahead` to `false` fails 10/13; swapping greater/less fails 7/13.

**Gates** — `cargo fmt --check` pass, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` pass, `cargo test --all-targets` **526 passed / 0 failed**, all `examples/*.rb` and `modules/*.rb` exit 0. **`./rbops/verify.sh` was not run: `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout** (same absence phase026 recorded) — reported honestly, not claimed.

**Docs** — `phases/phase-027/REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` (5 items with file:line: `isnt` still unparsed, `expect x is equal to be yes` ambiguity, `rb format` now normalising word forms to symbols, stale formatter comment, `test`-block scoping).
